From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Allow installing the C++ test suites

HOLOSCAN_BUILD_TESTS builds the test tree but no install component ships it,
leaving a distribution to copy binaries out of the build tree along with their
build-tree RPATH. Add HOLOSCAN_INSTALL_TESTS_DIR to opt into installing the
self-contained suites, so CMake places them and rewrites their RPATH as it does
for any other installed target.

The suites are the gtest programs of tests/, of the holoviz, vision and
inference modules, and of the holoviz operators. Where a directory also builds
programs that are not suites, such as tests/system's smoke programs or
tests/config's compile-only check, holoscan_install_test_targets() takes the
suites by name, since a runner executes every program it installs as one.

Some suites read files or exec programs by a compiled-in build-tree path, which
an installed suite cannot reach and which a distribution's QA rejects. Install
each beside the suite and compile in that path instead:
- holoviz_test_text_renderer_compare's monospace TTF;
- compile_test's golden plan artifacts, in compiler-testdata/;
- the child programs the channel suites exec, in channel/.
HOLOINFER_TEST reads its ONNX models relative to its working directory, so they
go to modules/inference/tests/test_models under the suites' directory.

The HoloMQ suites go to a holomq/ subdirectory. Their ctest entries split them
by gtest filter and run two child programs standalone, so they are replayed
entry by entry rather than run whole. holomq_cuda_unittests execs
holomq_cuda_host_import_child by a compiled-in path, which for an installed
suite has to be the installed child.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
